XFAR
====

DEFAULT BINDINGS
-----------------
  Super+D                      Open the launcher
  Super+Right / Super+Left     Grow / shrink the focused column
  Super+Up / Super+Down        Grow / shrink the focused window's height
  Super+Space                  Cycle windows through grid slots
  Super+Q                      Close the focused window
  Super+Shift+Q                Quit xfar
  Super+N                      Create and switch to a workspace
  Super+Tab / Super+Shift+Tab  Switch to the next / previous workspace
  Super+Shift+Right            Move the focused window to the next workspace
  Super+Shift+Left             Move the focused window to the previous workspace
  Alt+Tab                      Cycle tiled windows; release Alt to focus

Desktop bindings are configurable under [keybindings]. Alt+Tab is fixed.

LAYOUT
------
  Tiled toplevels use a balanced grid with ceil(sqrt(n)) columns and
  full-height column strips. Dialogs, modal toplevels, and fixed-size
  toplevels float centered. Fullscreen toplevels cover the output and hide
  the bar.

  [tiling] max_columns and max_rows set per-workspace capacity. A new tiled
  window that would exceed capacity moves to the next workspace only when it
  already exists; otherwise the current grid grows past the configured limit.
  min_width and min_height clamp divider movement.

  Workspaces are created at runtime. Empty inactive workspaces are retired.

CONFIGURATION
-------------
  Path: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xfar/config.toml
        ~/.config/xfar/config.toml when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset or empty

  Every field is optional. Unknown sections and keys are rejected. On the
  nested backend, malformed files are reported and xfar falls back to defaults.

  [keyboard]
  repeat_delay_ms = 200
  repeat_rate = 25

  [keybindings]
  launcher = "Super+D"
  grow_width = "Super+Right"
  shrink_width = "Super+Left"
  grow_height = "Super+Up"
  shrink_height = "Super+Down"
  cycle = "Super+Space"
  close = "Super+Q"
  quit = "Super+Shift+Q"
  new_workspace = "Super+N"
  next_workspace = "Super+Tab"
  prev_workspace = "Super+Shift+Tab"
  move_to_next_workspace = "Super+Shift+Right"
  move_to_prev_workspace = "Super+Shift+Left"

  [appearance]
  Color keys: background, panel, accent, text, placeholder,
              vdesktop_active, vdesktop, clock, switch_border
  Color format: "#rrggbb" or "#rrggbbaa"
  background_image = "/path/to/image"
  background_mode = "fit"    stretch | fit | center | tile
  panel_position = "top"     top | bottom

  Relative wallpaper paths resolve from xfar's working directory.

  [window]
  focus_new = true

  [tiling]
  min_width = 320
  min_height = 240
  max_columns = 3
  max_rows = 3

  [cursor]
  visible = true

  [screenshot]
  dir = "~/screenshots"

  [session]
  keep_state = true

  Session state is stored at $XDG_STATE_HOME/xfar/session.toml, or
  ~/.local/state/xfar/session.toml when XDG_STATE_HOME is unset or empty.

  Wallpapers are rasterized per output size and cached under
  $XDG_CACHE_HOME/xfar (usually ~/.cache/xfar). xfar validate checks the file
  without rewriting it.

RUNTIME
-------
  The default build uses the nested winit backend inside an existing X11 or
  Wayland session. A build with --features tty uses DRM/KMS, GBM, libinput,
  and libseat when neither WAYLAND_DISPLAY nor DISPLAY is set.

  The DRM/KMS backend requires seatd, a TTY, and /dev/dri. Screenshot capture
  is available only on this backend.

  XFAR_TERMINAL selects the terminal used to page help and validation output.
  The default is foot.

BUILT-IN COMMANDS
-----------------
  xfar.help        Page this manual
  xfar.settings    Edit the effective configuration; Ctrl+S saves
  xfar.validate    Page xfar validate output
  xfar.screenshot  Capture the composed output (DRM/KMS only)
  xfar.quit        Quit xfar
